 `tests/test_mariehamn_junction_review.py` checks that the review applies once and needs the fifth pass. It also checks that the compiler rejects an early western leg, a second carriageway present before 1995, double ownership, changed inputs and wrong counts.
+
+# 1942 approach traces reviewed against the orthophoto — 2026-11-12
+
+The city stage for 1942 (shown 1942–1967) included five hand traces of approach roads. They were drawn on the official orthophoto of 25 July 1942 in a 4 m/pixel view, with only 12–13 points for each road over 2–3 km. They were not attached to persistent objects, and from 1968 onward the parts outside the reviewed city area were still drawn, until 2013. This review covers three of the traces. It compares each with the original photo, fetched as georeferenced 2 m/pixel tiles (tile x = E // 512, y = N // 512 in EPSG:3874), with the 1968 NLS sheet 101208 and with today's roads.
+
+| Trace | Finding | Change |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Södra vägen på halvön, 1942 (1.93 km) | No road under the trace on the 1942 photo: south of the town edge it crosses continuous forest and rocky ground, and its northern end crosses ground that is built-up blocks by 1968. The 1968 map shows no road there either. The real 1942 road down the peninsula is the main road (Västra Ytternäsvägen), 100–330 m to the west. | Rejected. It is no longer drawn in the city stages or in the older-roads layer. Its original pixels stay in the trace files. |
+| Östra infarten norrifrån, 1942 (2.98 km) | A real road on the photo: Godbyvägen, the curve at Johannebo, past today's Grindmattesvägen and along Strandgatan into the town. The trace is a coarse chord, up to 20–60 m from the road's line. | 17 objects get the photo as evidence from 1942 and are drawn with their own centre lines. |
+| Västra infarten norrifrån, 1942 (2.75 km) | A real road on the photo: from the western edge to the bend, Svibyvägen, the diagonal to Klintvägen's straight northern part and Klintgränd, Västra Utfarten's diagonal and Ålandsvägen into the town. | 13 objects get the photo as evidence from 1942. |
+
+Where no persistent object matches the 1942 road, the 1942 and 1952 stages draw a short connecting piece (seven in all). Two of these follow the photo directly, because the coarse trace was 30–40 m off there:
+
+- Grindmattesvägen to Strandgatan;
+- Svibyvägen to Klintvägen.
+
+Their centre lines were retraced from the photo as a least-cost path over the pale road surface between the two object ends, simplified to 2 m and checked visually. The other gaps keep the reviewed trace remainder, with its ends moved onto the adjoining objects:
+
+- near the northern photo edge;
+- at Rökerirondellen;
+- the western stub at the bend;
+- at Klintgränd;
+- at Ålandsplan.
+
+The traces' last stretches into the town are not drawn. Östra's follows Strandgatan, which is already shown from 1861; Västra's deviates 30–50 m. From 1968 the dated objects alone show the roads, so no 1942 trace is drawn on top of them.
+
+Not backdated, with reasons in the review file:
+
+- Godbyvägen's northernmost object, which extends past the photo's edge;
+- the Godbyvägen–Bolstavägen junction pieces;
+- Skiljevägen (only its northern half follows the 1942 road);
+- the northernmost Strandgatan piece (`way-35011592`), which the 1942 city map's own Strandgatan trace already draws;
+- Nya Godbyvägen and Rökerirondellen (1978);
+- Stenhuggarvägen, whose northern end hooks west where the photo shows no road;
+- Svibyvägen's slip piece at the later Västra rondellen;
+- the Västra Utfarten stub and the split junction pieces at Ålandsplan.
+
+The photo dates presence in 1942, not construction.
+
+**Data and checks.** `data/mariehamn-approaches-1942.json` records the review: input hashes of the original traces, their city-stage copies and every object, the per-approach distance guards, and the retraced gaps. It is generated by `data/map-scan-cache/review/trace-1942/prepare.py` from the snapshot taken before the change. Keep the script for audit; do not rerun it blindly. The same folder holds:
+
+- the tile manifest;
+- the overlays (`sodra-*`, `ostra-*`, `vastra-*`, `retrace-*`, `result-1945.jpg`, `result-1970.jpg`);
+- `retrace.py`, `audit.py` and `scope-audit.json`.
+
+`scripts/mariehamn_approaches_1942.py` runs after the junction review. It validates everything before it changes the catalogue. It removes the rejected trace and the carried-over parts from 1968 onward, and prepends a 1942 open state and geometry period to each reviewed object. Those entries use the object's earliest geometry, so Klintvägen keeps its partial northern extent until its 1978 bend. It adds the gap pieces only to the 1942 and 1952 stages. `scripts/build_historical_roads.py` drops the rejected trace from the older-roads layer.
+
+The scope audit:
+
+- confirms that the baseline equals the snapshot;
+- confirms that exactly the 30 reviewed objects changed, each with its earlier states, periods, evidence and source links kept unchanged after the new 1942 entries;
+- confirms that no geometry changed;
+- confirms that in each city stage only the three trace features were removed.
+
+Earlier tests that asserted "absent the year before the first map edition" now allow this reviewed 1942 evidence (marker `approach1942`). The central-Strandgatan test still checks that the piece under the 1942 city trace is not backdated.
+
+`tests/mariehamn-approaches-1942.test.cjs` and `tests/test_mariehamn_approaches_1942.py` cover:
+
+- the rejection;
+- the absence of raw traces;
+- the 1942 starts and the kept dates;
+- the retraced gaps;
+- the compiler's refusals.
+
+The two other 1942 traces in the set (Förbindelse mellan infartsvägarna, Väg till västra stadskanten) are not reviewed here.
+
+**Publication (junction review and 1942 approach review).** Deployed together on 2026-11-12 as Cloudflare version `7c730ce9-4a66-4379-b989-eeb38575c641`, because the 1942 step runs after the junction review in the same build. The release was prepared from the live version (`04f931de…`) plus only these two reviews:
+
+- the catalogue;
+- `assets/mariehamn-junction-review.json` and `assets/mariehamn-approaches-1942.json`;
+- `assets/historical-roads.json` (only the rejected Södra trace removed);
+- the two loader cards in `index.html`;
+- cache stamps in `temporal-objects.js`, `object.html`, `historical-roads.js` and `object-page.js`.
+
+Other unpublished workspace changes were left out. All 226 relevant JavaScript tests passed against the release tree. All 290 live files were checked byte for byte against the release; see `deployment.json` in `junctions/` and in `trace-1942/`.
